WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.509 --> 00:00:02.665
- Don't get caught up
with your imagination

00:00:02.665 --> 00:00:04.447
to jump into it right away.

00:00:04.447 --> 00:00:06.114
Your first tiny step

00:00:07.122 --> 00:00:09.108
will make this all happen.

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:13.288
Don't feel that you have to
very smart to do something.

00:00:13.288 --> 00:00:16.585
Stupid people like us
do things, it works out.

00:00:16.585 --> 00:00:19.655
Because human beings are
not always about money.

00:00:19.655 --> 00:00:21.465
Human beings are much bigger than just

00:00:21.465 --> 00:00:22.654
money-making machine.

00:00:22.654 --> 00:00:25.799
All human beings in the
world are entrepreneurs.

00:00:25.799 --> 00:00:29.062
That's in our DNA. That's in our blood.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.910
She'll give your life to
make sure that trust is kept.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.352
We think making money is
the purpose of the life.

00:00:35.352 --> 00:00:36.591
Purpose of life is not making money.

00:00:36.591 --> 00:00:39.563
When you imagine, don't put a limit.

00:00:39.563 --> 00:00:41.919
Be as wide as you can be.

00:00:41.919 --> 00:00:44.265
All the thing that I see about the world,

00:00:44.265 --> 00:00:48.341
what it should be, it's all
question of imagination.

00:00:48.341 --> 00:00:50.069
- He's a Bangladeshi social entrepreneur,

00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:51.637
banker, and economist.

00:00:51.637 --> 00:00:53.670
He was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.239
for pioneering the concept of

00:00:55.239 --> 00:00:57.513
microcredit and microfinancing.

00:00:57.513 --> 00:00:59.103
He also serves on the board of directors

00:00:59.103 --> 00:01:01.106
of the United Nations Foundation.

00:01:01.106 --> 00:01:02.899
He's Muhammad Yunus and here is my take

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:05.566
on his top 10 rules for success.

00:01:08.325 --> 00:01:10.922
- Imagine big things, but always,

00:01:10.922 --> 00:01:14.830
this is my recommendation personally,

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:16.830
always start very small.

00:01:17.914 --> 00:01:20.328
As small as you can get.

00:01:20.328 --> 00:01:22.430
Don't get caught up with your imagination

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.237
to jump into it right away.

00:01:24.237 --> 00:01:28.154
Your first tiny step will
make this all happen.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:33.996
So, limit yourself into
tiny little thing of change.

00:01:33.996 --> 00:01:35.201
And make that happen.

00:01:35.201 --> 00:01:37.573
It's easy, it's not difficult if you make

00:01:37.573 --> 00:01:39.371
very simple, very easy.

00:01:39.371 --> 00:01:42.278
Don't get scared if you
don't know something.

00:01:42.278 --> 00:01:47.141
Don't feel that you have to
very smart to do something.

00:01:47.141 --> 00:01:51.780
Stupid people like us
do things, it works out.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.297
So, that's the fun part of it.

00:01:54.297 --> 00:01:57.555
Don't feel scared about
challenging things.

00:01:57.555 --> 00:02:00.745
Conventional bankers always telling me

00:02:00.745 --> 00:02:03.507
we can't lend money to the poor people.

00:02:03.507 --> 00:02:07.182
You know why? Because
they're not credit worthy.

00:02:07.182 --> 00:02:09.394
I have heard it millions of times

00:02:09.394 --> 00:02:11.890
telling me that they
are not credit-worthy.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:15.223
I wondered, should the banks tell people

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:20.146
whether they are credit worthy or not?

00:02:20.146 --> 00:02:23.112
Or that people should be telling the banks

00:02:23.112 --> 00:02:26.953
whether they are people-worthy or not?

00:02:26.953 --> 00:02:27.953
(audience claps)

00:02:27.953 --> 00:02:29.203
You reverse it.

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:35.495
You reverse the whole question.

00:02:35.495 --> 00:02:37.472
Then you get it.

00:02:37.472 --> 00:02:41.963
So, doing the opposite
way, doing the stupid way

00:02:41.963 --> 00:02:43.374
is not a bad thing.

00:02:43.374 --> 00:02:45.137
Everything that we do
in the business world

00:02:45.137 --> 00:02:46.389
is focused on making money.

00:02:46.389 --> 00:02:48.484
That's what the indicator that you

00:02:48.484 --> 00:02:51.918
try to assess how successful we are.

00:02:51.918 --> 00:02:54.243
In the business world
there's nothing else.

00:02:54.243 --> 00:02:56.031
So that kind of squeezed out all kinds

00:02:56.031 --> 00:03:00.093
of social orientation of
human life and human activity.

00:03:00.093 --> 00:03:02.107
And that's not a tenable situation.

00:03:02.107 --> 00:03:04.116
And that untenable situation is created

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:05.618
by the structure that we have.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.818
I said, business doesn't have to be always

00:03:07.818 --> 00:03:10.424
money-centered, always self-centered.

00:03:10.424 --> 00:03:13.845
All, many times obsessed with money.

00:03:13.845 --> 00:03:16.984
Because human beings are
not always about money.

00:03:16.984 --> 00:03:18.595
Human beings are much bigger than

00:03:18.595 --> 00:03:20.092
just money making machine.

00:03:20.092 --> 00:03:22.519
We are not robots. We are human beings.

00:03:22.519 --> 00:03:24.806
We take care of ourselves individually.

00:03:24.806 --> 00:03:27.064
At the same time, we take
care of everybody else.

00:03:27.064 --> 00:03:29.044
We take care of the planet itself.

00:03:29.044 --> 00:03:31.539
And business world doesn't
have that orientation.

00:03:31.539 --> 00:03:34.148
At the moment. We can do that.

00:03:34.148 --> 00:03:35.726
We can create different kind of business

00:03:35.726 --> 00:03:37.357
which is not money centered.

00:03:37.357 --> 00:03:40.188
The designing of education
system is very important.

00:03:40.188 --> 00:03:42.871
It's not, I tell again,
this is also relevant

00:03:42.871 --> 00:03:44.283
for education system.

00:03:44.283 --> 00:03:46.389
I tell that you don't have to wait

00:03:46.389 --> 00:03:48.993
to finally graduate, to finally
get your master's degree

00:03:48.993 --> 00:03:52.826
or whatever degree, to
become an entrepreneur.

00:03:53.672 --> 00:03:56.299
You can become entrepreneur
anytime you want.

00:03:56.299 --> 00:03:58.429
Any class you are in, whether it's junior,

00:03:58.429 --> 00:04:00.830
high school or senior high
school, doesn't matter.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.539
'Cuz you are an entrepreneur.

00:04:02.539 --> 00:04:05.079
You don't wait for a certificate.

00:04:05.079 --> 00:04:07.238
You wait for a certificate when you are

00:04:07.238 --> 00:04:08.527
look for a job because you need

00:04:08.527 --> 00:04:10.269
these piece of paper to get in.

00:04:10.269 --> 00:04:13.426
This is your entry document to get in.

00:04:13.426 --> 00:04:15.102
But entrepreneur doesn't need it.

00:04:15.102 --> 00:04:16.799
That doesn't mean that
you don't need education.

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:18.747
You need education to the extent

00:04:18.747 --> 00:04:20.415
that you are interested in,

00:04:20.415 --> 00:04:21.872
not because of a certificate.

00:04:21.872 --> 00:04:24.448
So, certificate orientation can go,

00:04:24.448 --> 00:04:25.926
if you are an entrepreneur.

00:04:25.926 --> 00:04:28.382
And make sure what are
the things interest you

00:04:28.382 --> 00:04:31.074
and get to those kind of educations.

00:04:31.074 --> 00:04:34.067
Who told you to have jobs?

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:37.724
Did your teacher tell you to have jobs?

00:04:37.724 --> 00:04:40.303
Did you read it in your textbooks?

00:04:40.303 --> 00:04:43.635
Of course they cannot
answer that question.

00:04:43.635 --> 00:04:45.573
I said forget about jobs.

00:04:45.573 --> 00:04:48.180
Job is a very old-fashioned idea.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.347
Obsolete idea.

00:04:51.145 --> 00:04:54.610
That should have ended
in the last century,

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:57.543
but somehow it sneaked in.

00:04:57.543 --> 00:04:59.167
Get rid of it.

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:02.314
You keep telling yourself again and again,

00:05:02.314 --> 00:05:05.990
I'm not a job seeker, I am a job creator.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.500
And behave like a job creator,
think like a job creator.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.349
Suddenly you see
completely different thing

00:05:11.349 --> 00:05:12.688
emerging in front of you.

00:05:12.688 --> 00:05:14.951
It's in your head, which causes a problem,

00:05:14.951 --> 00:05:16.629
not in your ability.

00:05:16.629 --> 00:05:19.380
You have the ability
to become entrepreneur.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.781
And I tell them that all human beings

00:05:21.781 --> 00:05:24.021
in the world are entrepreneurs.

00:05:24.021 --> 00:05:27.511
That's in our DNA. That's in our blood.

00:05:27.511 --> 00:05:29.438
That's how millions of years we've lived

00:05:29.438 --> 00:05:33.249
in this planet by using
that entrepreneurship.

00:05:33.249 --> 00:05:35.358
When we were in the caves,

00:05:35.358 --> 00:05:38.191
we're not sending job applications

00:05:39.312 --> 00:05:42.645
from cave number five to cave number 15.

00:05:43.571 --> 00:05:45.629
Do you have a job for me?

00:05:45.629 --> 00:05:49.505
We created a tradition of go-getters.

00:05:49.505 --> 00:05:53.668
We are go-getters. We are problem solvers.

00:05:53.668 --> 00:05:56.012
Some people mistaken it,

00:05:56.012 --> 00:05:58.248
convert it into job-seekers

00:05:58.248 --> 00:06:02.102
as if human beings are not
born to work for somebody else.

00:06:02.102 --> 00:06:04.517
Human beings much bigger than that.

00:06:04.517 --> 00:06:08.420
But the moment you accept
a job, you limit yourself.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:11.589
Your life is made into tiny little thing.

00:06:11.589 --> 00:06:14.195
Which yourself is huge big thing.

00:06:14.195 --> 00:06:17.807
Your creative power can
go any direction you want.

00:06:17.807 --> 00:06:19.425
That's what you should be.

00:06:19.425 --> 00:06:22.245
- Who have you seen as
an inspirational figure?

00:06:22.245 --> 00:06:24.356
- Well, I'm sure many people.

00:06:24.356 --> 00:06:28.532
Probably in the early stage
when I was growing up,

00:06:28.532 --> 00:06:30.851
I would say my mother was my inspiration

00:06:30.851 --> 00:06:34.934
because she didn't go to
school, study very much.

00:06:35.854 --> 00:06:38.459
4th grade, 5th grade, probably.

00:06:38.459 --> 00:06:40.442
That's all the education she had.

00:06:40.442 --> 00:06:42.248
But very unique character.

00:06:42.248 --> 00:06:44.831
Very open, very helping person.

00:06:46.211 --> 00:06:50.020
She always inspired me in
that, whatever that she did.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:52.682
The other one inspiration I get from

00:06:52.682 --> 00:06:54.764
the people that I work
with, all these women

00:06:54.764 --> 00:06:56.368
that work in the village.

00:06:56.368 --> 00:06:58.201
How hard their life is

00:07:01.291 --> 00:07:02.910
and how they work so hard

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:05.106
to make a little difference in their life.

00:07:05.106 --> 00:07:07.137
To make sure their children don't have

00:07:07.137 --> 00:07:08.829
to go through the misery that she has

00:07:08.829 --> 00:07:11.408
gone through, that's
the only thing she does.

00:07:11.408 --> 00:07:13.648
And she's so committed, given this tiny

00:07:13.648 --> 00:07:16.058
money she gets in her hand.

00:07:16.058 --> 00:07:20.157
She tries to get the best
mileage out of this money.

00:07:20.157 --> 00:07:23.004
When she receive this first money,

00:07:23.004 --> 00:07:25.459
when you give her loan from Grameen Bank,

00:07:25.459 --> 00:07:27.221
as I said, initial loan being about

00:07:27.221 --> 00:07:30.015
30 dollars or 35 dollars,

00:07:30.015 --> 00:07:33.149
when she holds this money
she literally shakes,

00:07:33.149 --> 00:07:35.104
she cannot stand still because

00:07:35.104 --> 00:07:36.469
she did not believe anybody could

00:07:36.469 --> 00:07:39.692
trust her with such an
enormous amount of money.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:42.173
She thinks this is such a huge money,

00:07:42.173 --> 00:07:44.310
she doesn't know how to handle that money.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.580
So, that's what the shaking part comes.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:49.689
And inside of her she keeps promising

00:07:49.689 --> 00:07:52.533
anybody who has trusted her all this money

00:07:52.533 --> 00:07:55.726
didn't ask for anything,
just gave her the money

00:07:55.726 --> 00:07:57.621
on the basis of their trust.

00:07:57.621 --> 00:07:59.287
She will give her life to make sure

00:07:59.287 --> 00:08:01.656
that trust is kept.

00:08:01.656 --> 00:08:05.239
And her eyes will be,
tears will be running

00:08:06.169 --> 00:08:10.569
down from her eyes not
believing that it's real.

00:08:10.569 --> 00:08:12.934
It's not a dream, it's a real thing.

00:08:12.934 --> 00:08:14.981
And the rest of her life she struggles

00:08:14.981 --> 00:08:17.630
to make sure she makes that thing true

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:20.631
that yes, her trust will never be broken.

00:08:20.631 --> 00:08:22.200
And that's what keeps the whole

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.617
Grameen bank microcredit together,

00:08:24.617 --> 00:08:27.659
the relationship of trust between the two.

00:08:27.659 --> 00:08:29.804
We think making money is
the purpose of the life.

00:08:29.804 --> 00:08:32.262
Purpose of life is not making money.

00:08:32.262 --> 00:08:33.682
Purpose of life is to make oneself happy

00:08:33.682 --> 00:08:36.123
and the rest of the world happy.

00:08:36.123 --> 00:08:37.760
But that purpose is forgotten,

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:40.095
so we have to reinvent the purpose.

00:08:40.095 --> 00:08:41.457
What is the purpose of our life?

00:08:41.457 --> 00:08:43.140
That's what the young
people are looking for.

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:44.941
Human life is about creativity,

00:08:44.941 --> 00:08:48.266
about doing things so
that it becomes a legacy,

00:08:48.266 --> 00:08:50.266
build a legacy for yourself.

00:08:50.266 --> 00:08:52.607
That's not what we do in business.

00:08:52.607 --> 00:08:54.336
In business, we have a big, big

00:08:54.336 --> 00:08:57.842
stack of cash and that's where
I'm going to say goodbye.

00:08:57.842 --> 00:08:59.922
We have the capacity to change that thing.

00:08:59.922 --> 00:09:02.646
Nobody should be unemployed,
nobody should be poor.

00:09:02.646 --> 00:09:03.960
It's for the same reason.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.065
We are capable.

00:09:05.065 --> 00:09:07.905
Nobody should be wealthy and dependent.

00:09:07.905 --> 00:09:10.405
Imagination is the real power.

00:09:13.136 --> 00:09:16.136
I imagine about the app to transport

00:09:18.851 --> 00:09:20.351
me into your site.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:25.407
All the crazy things
that you can think about.

00:09:25.407 --> 00:09:28.664
When you imagine, don't put a limit.

00:09:28.664 --> 00:09:31.263
Be as wide as you can be

00:09:31.263 --> 00:09:33.538
in creating the image of the world

00:09:33.538 --> 00:09:35.268
that you want to create.

00:09:35.268 --> 00:09:39.726
Without any hesitation,
without any limitation.

00:09:39.726 --> 00:09:43.105
Be as wide as you can
be in your imagination.

00:09:43.105 --> 00:09:46.520
As if you are writing a social fiction.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.774
We like science fiction all the time.

00:09:48.774 --> 00:09:52.803
But unfortunately we don't
write social fictions.

00:09:52.803 --> 00:09:55.674
Fictions are the driving force,

00:09:55.674 --> 00:09:58.723
like in science, in
technology, science fiction

00:09:58.723 --> 00:09:59.957
becomes a driving force.

00:09:59.957 --> 00:10:01.644
It makes things happen.

00:10:01.644 --> 00:10:04.602
Similarly, if you have
done the social fiction,

00:10:04.602 --> 00:10:06.249
it will make it happen.

00:10:06.249 --> 00:10:08.294
- Let's imagine that I was one of

00:10:08.294 --> 00:10:12.526
Grameen Bank's clients
and I have the loan.

00:10:12.526 --> 00:10:16.463
But what mindset do I need
for myself to succeed?

00:10:16.463 --> 00:10:19.435
- Well, succeed that you take a loan

00:10:19.435 --> 00:10:20.703
to start a business, that's what you

00:10:20.703 --> 00:10:23.690
explained to the bank
that this is what I'll do.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:25.495
And you'll focus on that that I

00:10:25.495 --> 00:10:27.462
have to be successful in this

00:10:27.462 --> 00:10:29.757
and make sure that I can pay back

00:10:29.757 --> 00:10:31.271
all the money out of the income that I

00:10:31.271 --> 00:10:34.865
make out of the investment that I did.

00:10:34.865 --> 00:10:36.897
And that focus is very important

00:10:36.897 --> 00:10:39.124
and self-confidence that I can do it.

00:10:39.124 --> 00:10:42.892
Because many borrowers, maybe like you,

00:10:42.892 --> 00:10:44.156
never had any experience before.

00:10:44.156 --> 00:10:45.753
Taking money from somebody else

00:10:45.753 --> 00:10:47.477
and doing things and paying back.

00:10:47.477 --> 00:10:50.133
They never handled money in many cases

00:10:50.133 --> 00:10:52.130
because their husbands handled the money.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.703
The first time they are handling money,

00:10:53.703 --> 00:10:55.376
so they are scared to death.

00:10:55.376 --> 00:10:57.374
So, have confidence, make it happen,

00:10:57.374 --> 00:11:00.316
go step by step and then, once you have

00:11:00.316 --> 00:11:03.161
been successful in getting the money back,

00:11:03.161 --> 00:11:05.172
you become very confident, you did it.

00:11:05.172 --> 00:11:07.021
'Cuz you go through the whole process,

00:11:07.021 --> 00:11:08.385
became more successful.

00:11:08.385 --> 00:11:10.721
That builds up tremendous
amount of success.

00:11:10.721 --> 00:11:12.964
What the thing that I see about the world,

00:11:12.964 --> 00:11:16.229
what it should be, is all
a question of imagination.

00:11:16.229 --> 00:11:18.896
(serious music)

00:11:23.011 --> 00:11:26.600
If we imagine today what
kind of world we want

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:29.683
and that's the world will be created.

00:11:30.651 --> 00:11:34.666
Everybody has freedom to
imagine in his or her way.

00:11:34.666 --> 00:11:37.851
My imagination is we
want to create a world

00:11:37.851 --> 00:11:42.048
which will be absolutely
free from poverty.

00:11:42.048 --> 00:11:44.345
Meaning that there'll be no poor person

00:11:44.345 --> 00:11:47.428
on this planet anywhere in the world.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:52.597
And once we create that,
we'll create poverty museums.

00:11:53.545 --> 00:11:55.513
So that people who'd like to know

00:11:55.513 --> 00:11:58.049
what is it that used to be called poverty?

00:11:58.049 --> 00:11:59.248
How did it happen?

00:11:59.248 --> 00:12:01.621
So, they will go into poverty museum,

00:12:01.621 --> 00:12:03.154
they take their children
to poverty museum.

00:12:03.154 --> 00:12:05.409
That's the kind of the world
that I would like to build.

00:12:05.409 --> 00:12:07.087
And that will be the world where

00:12:07.087 --> 00:12:09.403
there'll be no unemployment.

00:12:09.403 --> 00:12:11.434
And when you tell people, oh, they used to

00:12:11.434 --> 00:12:14.084
unemployment, there was a big crisis,

00:12:14.084 --> 00:12:15.694
there's a lot of unemployed people

00:12:15.694 --> 00:12:17.230
and the young unemployed.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:20.364
And people will be wondering,
what is unemployment?

00:12:20.364 --> 00:12:22.387
Why should anybody be unemployed?

00:12:22.387 --> 00:12:23.970
They have capacity.

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:28.626
Why a one human being
should be unemployed?

00:12:28.626 --> 00:12:30.257
What does it mean?

00:12:30.257 --> 00:12:32.847
(serious music)

00:12:32.847 --> 00:12:33.887
They'll be writing thesis to

00:12:33.887 --> 00:12:35.998
understand what is unemployment,

00:12:35.998 --> 00:12:39.215
why did it happen those past years.

00:12:39.215 --> 00:12:41.606
